## Unlimited Power
- Prowess can now go up to 1000 in PoD
- Balanced the splats around this new limit
- The short version of it is that lower levels change little (vanilla prowess challenges, mortals, hunters, young vamps etc) while the higher levels scale harder (elder disciplines, high dharma, high integrity etc) making the gap between a newly embraced vamp and a 4th generation methuselah wider as an example

## (Almost) No Levies Integration
- The No Levies game rule has been removed
- Levies have been renamed to Mortal Rabble to represented that they aren't conscripted peasants and that they are weak
- Levies numbers have been reduced significantly
- Garrison numbers have also been reduced quite a bit

## AI improvements
- Fixed and updated AI building weights for Vampire, Ghoul, and Revenant buildings
- Vampires don't value the generic Mob MAA so highly anymore
- Fixed AI building weight for special buildings being very high which made the AI unable to build anything if they owned one
- Significant AI Improvements for all Fera:
	- Building logic greatly improved, AI will prioritize buildings that keep it economically stable and fits its personality. They will also avoid niche buildings that the AI cannot properly utilize.
	- Fera Buildings now have proper Vassal Directives weights, making the AI actually build the relevant buildings when told to.
	- Domicile Buildings logic added. This only affects Mokolé since the others do not have domiciles yet.
	- The AI has realized it has supernatural powers and shouldn't spend most of its time studying how to talk to people better (will now prioritize Fera lifestyles over vanilla ones. Meaning they will naturally obtain perks in their Gift lifestyles)
	- The AI has learned how to get trait xp and thus increase in Fera Rank. They have access to all player sources of xp, and additionally have a chance of receiving xp over time depending on various factors.
	- Ancestor Spirits will seek out AI members of their dynasty to Pact with over time.
	- The below are locked behind reaching a certain Fera Rank
	- Rank 2: now simulate Umbra exploration, allowing them to gain Planetary Gifts, find wandering Spirits, and all the Wyrm Fera mechanics.
	- Rank 3: can now make pacts with Spirits they find in the Umbra or ones they summoned themselves. They will also perform Chiminage to strengthen them.
	- Rank 3: will go on Spirit Quests to find new Fetish artifacts and gain Wisdom renown.
	- Rank 4: will now join existing Fera Coteries or create their own. They can also invite other Fera of any rank into their coterie. These are restricted to characters in the same or neighboring realms
	- Rank 4: train with their pack with all the benefits it can give, including choosing a Pack Totem

## Gameplay additions
- Added a new PoD bloodline, the Erk, to give more depth to the vast steppes
- Added Artifact Power mechanic: All forging nodes add artifact power during crafting, the value is only shown if the forged artifact uses the mechanic. The value is used in the artifact's special effects if any.
- Fallen Hunter event: When a Hunter becomes a Vampire, Ghoul or public Infernalist, the game now acknowledges it with an event. You can either go landless (with the DLC), lose all your duchy+ titles to a Hunter vassal and go independent, or fight all your Hunter vassals at the same time in a civil war
- Added a decision for Wu T'ian to summon a Shih to help achieve their objective
- The "Heightened Fatality" game rule now also makes AI vampires diablerize their prisoners, assuming it fits their personality
- Added Sielanic Thaumaturgy as a new Blood Sorcery tradition
- Emma-o characters can now ask for a Shikome during the "Look for successor" decision 
- Added a new Mokolé MAA for the Osirian League
- Added Balefire damage. In addition to being treated as Aggravated Damage, it increases the time to naturally convert Aggravated to Superficial
- Added a new faith tenet to Devil Tiger KJ faiths

