# Princes of Darkness, "Blood & Silk", Version 1.18.1.1 11/13/2025

- Compatibility with Crusader Kings III 1.18.1.1 Crane Hotfix and All Under Heaven DLC

## Gameplay additions
- Added an experimental game rule that gives AI rulers free men-at-arms at regular intervals (as long as they have some income to spare). This is a bandaid fix for a vanilla AUH bug that prevents AI characters from recruiting new men-at-arms after the start of the game. You can change this game rule in an ongoing save. There are also additional options to give the AI a 50% or 90% discount on men-at-arms maintenance

## Gameplay changes
- Spirit Companions are now exempt from Knight Loyalty
- The Consolidate China CB will now be available after Hongben's death #This will allow China to be much more dynamic and much more likely to reunite post YEC collapse
- Piyau is now scripted bisexual #Use men as breeding stock and aggressively pleasure women was sadly not an option
- Levies are now less costly to maintain when raised #Levies are kind of an AI/noob trap, so making them cheaper ease that concern 
- The "too few spouses" piety penalty has been removed 
- KJ pregnancies are no longer five time at risk of miscarriages. KJ now have a fertility malus in their base trait.  #Representing the KJ complicated pregnancies as miscarriages is more faithful to the lore but also more annoying gameplay wise, risking ending with dozens miscarriages ballooning the dynasty trees

## Interface
- Overhauled the bookmark map and portrait graphics
- Added a "Choose Sifu" button to the character window sidebar so you can choose dead characters to be related to as custom Kuei-jin
- Edited the House Relations tooltip to clarify that the "Eradicate House" CB is disabled

## Bugfixes
- County religions now get set up during the first loading screen instead of afterwards (no more vanilla religions in Asia on day 1)
- Disabled the Chinese Great Projects from vanilla
- The new culture tradition Scholar Officials will no longer increase the success of learning Spirit Languages if the Spirit is Han
- Fixed Bastet Tribal Gifts focus not showing
- Fixed the silk road buildings never being allowed 
- Replaced an useless option in the Kizoku objective by an useful one 
- Fixed issues in Zheng, Jiang and Indraja lineages
- Fixed the Knossos labyrinth being so dreadful that it looped you back into being not dreadful at all
- Fixed the DLC requirements for the Adventurer bookmark


