# Princes of Darkness, "To Your Health and Good Spirits!", Version 1.17.0 9/9/2025
- Compatibility with Crusader Kings III 1.17.0 Ascendant and Coronations DLC

## Coronations
- Compatibility with Coronations DLC and patch. Coronations themselves are disabled in PoD

## Known bugs
- The option to travel with your landless camp during a Journey leads to broken events. It has been disabled until a more comprehensive fix can be found

## Health tracks
- Reworked wounds to be more in line with tabletop, using a combination of V20 and V5 rules. Damage can be superficial or aggravated, and if you get a wound trait, your health track is displayed in its tooltip
- Wound traits now have an experience track, representing your level of impairment
- The length of your health track is based on your splat:
  - 8 boxes: Werewolves
  - 7 boxes: Bastet, Demons, True Fae
  - 6 boxes: Vampires, Kuei-Jin, Risen
  - 5 boxes: Ghouls, Mummies, Wraiths
  - 4 boxes: Everyone else
- Wearing armor or having certain perks and abilities now lets you soak superficial damage, giving you a percentage chance to avoid all damage from one source
- Adapted all sources of wounds and wound healing (both PoD and vanilla) to the new system
- The Blood Potency modifiers now show in their tooltips how much superficial damage you can heal at once via Blood Heal

## Energy refactor
- Realm perks no longer act as a hard requirement on Fae cantrips. Instead, each perk you're missing increases the cantrip's Glamour cost by 1
- Every character now only has one "mana bar". Some examples:
  - Abominations and ghouled Shapeshifters use Gifts with Blood instead of Gnosis
  - Decani use Arcana and Lores with Blood instead of Resolve
  - Ghouled Changelings and Kinain Revenants use Arts with Blood instead of Glamour
  - Numina are now used with splat-appropriate resources (e.g. Bastet cast Sorcery with Gnosis)
  - The Yama King modifier (from the Akuma objective) now makes your character use Dread as a resource
- Blood-drinking effects are now consistent between all splats:
  - Kuei-Jin and Bane Mummies lose Mental Strain when hunting
  - Kuei-Jin gain a little Dharma experience when drinking blood, as long as their Dharma allows for it (now from any source, not just the Hunt Journey)
  - Kuei-Jin can now use the Exsanguination execution option
- Epiphanies can now only be used by characters who use Glamour as a resource
- Hsien now use Glamour instead of Chi
- Spending more energy than you have left now causes you superficial damage (should only happen in rare cases)
- The Enchanted trait was turned into a modifier and no longer gives you a Glamour bar
- Energy Vessels now only function as such if you fulfill the artifact's primary requirements
- Fixed various bugs with Energy Vessels
- Fixed a number of spells from Blood Sorcery, Necromancy, and Sorcery that were showing the wrong cost in the GUI
- Tweaked a number of tooltips for clarification when hunger can't be reduced due to blood potency effects

## Fera Rework
- Huge refactor of all internal fera code to make future additions possible
- Removed Rage
- Shapeshifting now costs Gnosis
- Clicking the Gnosis bar will bring up the Shapeshift menu
- Returning to Homid form now costs nothing
- Reworked Shapeshift form modifiers
- Various QoL improvements to the Shapeshift menu
- Removed Metis traits and lifestyle perks
- Disabled unimplemented Fera
- Hid unusable lifestyle focuses in Fera trees
- Bastet Crinos form now gives full Delirium
- Improved First Change process. Players have a higher chance of having Fera children.
- Changed Werewolf trait rank modifiers
- Changed Bastet trait rank modifiers
- All Bastet now start with Spirit Wilds "Access", meaning they can see the umbra window but not explore unless they are Swara or Rank 2 in their trait.
- Slightly increased Werewolf and Bastet base prowess to compensate for the loss of the Rage modifiers
- Slightly reduced Werewolf and Bastet lifespan
- Improved Beastborn adoption event chain and fixed bugs
- Reworked Fera Renown(trait xp): New methods for earning xp for each renown type. Changed ranking up decision requirements.
- Bastet Pryio now affect which Renown gets boosted
- Added new Power and Infamy renown types to Black Spiral Dancers
- Objectives now give 10 Renown instead of 1
- Reworked Train with Pack Journey: Removed lifestyle xp. Improved Prowess, war, and capital dev removal options. Added options to increase both yours and your Coterie's stats up to highest among the Coterie.
- Reworked Spirit Quests: Now a completely new Journey available to all Fera. Has multiple difficulties and scaling rewards including lifestyle xp, traits, and artifacts.
- Reworked Gnosis Regen: Chances are lower, making the use and loss of Gnosis more impactful.
- Reworked Accolades: Slightly buffed all of them. Renamed Pack Leader accolade to War Leader and made it available for Bastet as well.
- Fera can now pick higher tiers of court amenities
- Fera can now create cadet houses
- Coterie Totem modifiers now get removed/added to characters leaving/joining the coterie
- Totem modifiers rebalanced
- Renamed most instances of "Shapeshifters" or "Shifters" to "Fera" for clarity and consistency
- Renamed Litany government to Fera Tribe
- Added Primal Wolf and Kheuar languages to Werewolves and Bastet respectively
- Added Golems as recruitable MAA to the Shantar's Loom Planetary Gift
- Religions and faiths:
  - Moved all Wyrm worshipping faiths to the Wyrm religion
  - Moved all Bastet faiths to the new Feline religion
  - Renamed the Ronin religion to Outcasts
  - Overhauled Triat Alignment Doctrines
  - Overhauled all faith hostility and related doctrines, relations should be clearer now
  - Renamed Garou Nation doctrine to Litany and reworked its effects
  - Reworked Dark Litany doctrine
  - Added Karoush doctrine to Bastet faiths
  - Added Fallen Tribe doctrine to Wyrm faiths
  - Added Garou/Bastet/Wyrm Pacts doctrines to some other faiths to manage relationship exceptions
  - Renamed The Wyrm faith to Wyrm-bound
  - Added a new faith Velvet Brood to the Gaia religion, this is an unplayable faith made for Spirits
  - Reworked base virtues and sins for all religions
  - Overhauled all basic doctrines for all religions (crimes, splat relations, clerical functions, etc)
  - Removed Vampire doctrines (like blood sorcery)
  - Removed other redundant doctrines
  - Reworked many faiths' tenets
- Buildings:
  - All buildings have had their costs, requirements, and modifiers reworked
  - Kinfolk buildings: Cost gold and some minor prestige. Give minor amounts of supply limit. 
  - Werewolf buildings: Cost prestige and some gold. T1 can always be built regardless of development. All buildings reduce development in the province.
  - Bastet buildings: Cost prestige and some gold. Ignore all lower than X development requirements.
  - Werewolf/Bastet Tribe specific buildings: Cost prestige and piety. Converted into a 3 tier building.
  - Duchy Capitals: Cost prestige and some gold. Bastet ignore lower than X development requirements.
  - Special Buildings: Cost prestige and piety.
  - Added 3 new buildings. One for each Triat Alignment doctrine. Wyrm Taint building has been reworked to fit with the rest.
- MAA:
  - Rebalanced all Fera and Kinfolk MAA
  - Fera MAA now cost prestige to recruit and maintain
  - Stormcrows and Whitewolves now cost piety to recruit and gold to maintain
  - Replaced Black Spiral Dancer's Maniacs unlock with the new Children of Cluid MAA

## Spirits Rework
- Charms have been removed
- Nushi Spirits have been removed
- 26 new types of Spirits have been added
- Fera of sufficient Rank have a chance to turn into Ancestor Spirits upon death
- Added 6 Spirit Languages and a new interaction to learn them, this uses the Learn Language scheme. You need to know a Spirit's language to unlock further interactions.
- Spirits follow one of two Spirit only faiths and can no longer be converted or be made into cultists or neteru
- Asking for a Spirit Pact has had its acceptance factors overhauled
- Spirits now have a trait track representing their Rank. They only gain xp by character interactions from their companion.
- Every type of Spirit has its own Spirit Pact modifier and you gain an additional stack of it for every Rank the Spirit has
- All Spirits increase the Gnosis Regen of their companion
- Consolidated all seperate effects of hurting/imprisoning/etc spirits into a single effect
- Consolidated all interactions(except a sorcery spell) that summon a spirit into a single new character interaction
- Removed gold cost for hurting spirits
- Spirits cannot be Councillors or hold Court Positions
- Added new modifiers related to Spirits and their effects
- Wandering Gaian Spirits can now be found in the Spirit Wilds as expedition rewards

## Fetish Artifacts Rework
- Fetish artifacts now have an icon and game concept in their name to differentiate them
- Each equipped Fetish reduces a Fera's Gnosis Regen
- Fetish artifacts now require 5 or more Gnosis Regen to remain active, for non Fera they require a Spirit companion per fetish artifact
- Added 5 new fetish artifacts obtained from Fera Spirit Quests

## Mummy Rework
- Reworked all lifestyles, character interactions, and objectives
- Added a Hideout domicile with branching building upgrades, representing your tomb
- Enabled landless play for Mummies
- Added Memory, a measure of how much a Mummy remembers of their ancient culture of origin. Memory is a requirement for higher-level perks and interactions
- Added Integrity, a humanity-style system of morality for certain Mummy types. Low Integrity will lead to hefty penalties when resurrecting
- Removed Sekhem
- Added a repeatable Journey for learning True Names
- Added Wu T'ian replacement for Ushabti, Terracottan Army 
- (Wu Kuei are still unplayable)

## Ashirra Rework
- Removed Tariq el-Shaitan, Tariq el-Tanaqud, and Asdiqa al-Layl faiths
- All remaining faiths:
  - Reworked base religion doctrines
  - Reworked individual doctrines to differentiate them
  - Reworked all their tenets and added 2 new Ashirra specific ones
  - Reworked all holy sites
  - Reworked starting character and province faith setup
  - Reworked all sins and virtues
- Added new MAA, Sons of Sasan
- Replaced most vanilla holy order names with new ashirra ones
- Ashirra holy orders now use Ashirra MAA instead of Teutonic Knights
- Reworked the Ashirra unique building
- Added new travel option: the Hajji
- Added flavored title and character names, mostly like vanilla Islam and Arabian cultural names
- Added new flavorized title to Mesopotamia for Khaled/Shepherds of Islam
- Renamed the Ashirra Caliphate title
- Added Second Embrace childe education event
- Added Sihr Blood Magic
- Added new doctrine for Blood Magic in the Ashirra: Kufr, makes learning non-Sihr BM cost piety and give a timed negative modifier on completion.
- Made Sihr and Thaumaturgy incompatible and added clear tooltips about it
- Added Willing Embrace mechanic
- Modified existing Ashirra objectives
- Added 2 new Ashirra objectives
- Disabled zeal mechanic
- Religion and faith localization revised
- Various other related localization changes and improvements
- Count Junius now follows Via Regalis and has a unique modifier to represent the Ashirra's respect for him

## Kuei-Jin additions
- Reworked Kuei-Jin abilities. Kuei-Jin and Dhampyr now have 4 categories of powers:
  - Demon Arts, from Relentless Age. They are simple and have strong, stackable bonuses, but will have long-term ramifications for your Dharma gains
  - Soul Arts, from Relentless Age. They have a large number of perks that can be taken without prerequisites, but many of them cost more than one perk point
  - Chi Arts, based on a variety of KOTE disciplines. They give specialized bonuses, but have to be learned via Journey like Cainite Disciplines
  - Shintai, based on the Godbodies from Relentless Age. They're even more specialized, but come with Dharma requirements
- KJ can now be played landless
- Cleared up the tooltips for Dharma experience. Sources of Dharma experience are now shown in the trait itself, rather in the nested trait level tooltip
- Changes to KJ court positions, most notably adding scarlet screens positions that can only be filled by mortals, hence making it worthwhile to compete for GPs
- Reworked and added a lot to the KJ dynasty trees, adding house modifiers as well
- Added three dynasty legacies lines for the KJ
- Added a lot of new artifacts for the KJ
- The Dragon Nest ducal building has been expanded to 7 levels (instead of 3).
- Directions (a tenet that each Dharma has) now gives specific bonus to the Dragon Nest building depending #So KJ faith will have slightly different ducal buildings, depending on their direction 
- The Low War building now interacts with KJ dynasty legacies. 3 perks will improve this building in various ways 
- Added new MaA for the various kuei-jin dharmas
- Many new lore buttons for KJ
- The various "News From China" events have been removed  #You will obviously be able to play these events and not just read about them in the future
- The White Tiger Court objective has been updated to work with the new setup 
- Polished some unclear tooltips in the KJ dharma objectives
- The Quincunx interface has been disabled  #It will obviously need a complete rewrite to account for Asia 
- The Dharma gains have been overall reduced #the initial numbers were already generous and we added new ways to multiply them (artifacts) with more to come so it's needed to keep dharma being a serious commitment 
- Some dharmas now have an "unproven dharma" doctrine with reduce dharma gain #a big plot point in lore is that some dharmas never had recorded ascension to the hundred clouds thus stand on very shaky grounds
- If a character with an unproven dharma reaches dharma 10, the unproven dharma doctrine gets removed 
- Dharma using characters now will lose dharma trait experience when stress breaking (representing the tabletop Diao, the moments of blindness)
- Dhampyrs now visually age slower (since they do in lore)
- Kuei jin will now get the "main" great person localization instead of the generic one  #KJ will be the main splat of Asia and even though some GP loca doesn't completely match them, having all of the GPs loca be generic would be a bigger shame
- Reworked the KJ adoption mechanic #It is now a mix of the Giovanni mechanic and the vampire education one instead of being Fae reweawing
- Glossary of complicated or unusual terms used by the KJ is now available by tooltips in the texts
- Sun Li has been added to the adventurers bookmark
- Kuei-jin that somehow end up with a western Demon religion can now get dharma experience from the same sources as a Screamer would (killing and heinous acts)
- The way of the ten thousand screams has been reworked into a religion with the multiple yama kings as faiths. They have all specific dharma associated with them.
- Added two dhampyrs exclusive objectives
- Added pity insight after losing dharma level for AI

