## Numina tweaks
- Theurgy rework
  - Reworked all Theurgy perks
  - Theurgy can now only be learned by splats that can learn Sorcery and have a faith with Abrahamic roots. Samuel Haight mode lifts the faith requirement
  - Theurgy is now replaced with Blood Sorcery upon the embrace, like linear Sorcery
- Removed Lament since it's from 1999

## Crafting
- Nerfed Crafter trait
- Nerfed base crafting nodes
- Made base nodes visible in the crafting GUI
- Improvements to crafting game concepts
- Maximum durability now determines a forged artifact's rarity
- Fetishsmithing has been reworked: You now require either a Spirit Companion or imprisoned Spirit. Effects have been changed to account for the new spirits rework. It's forge node is automatically unlocked if you can equip fetishes. Enhancing node has been removed. The node can only be used once per forge session.

## Gameplay additions
- Added a Cult Leader court position for Demons that automatically converts vassals and courtiers (both yours and those of your Thralls) to your cult. Wars no longer convert new vassals to your cult automatically
- Added an experimental game rule to increase the chance of knights dying in battle. This can also be changed during an ongoing save
- Added an experimental game rule to remove all baronies from the game
- Added a Random option to the Endgame Delay game rule
- Added an option for Vampires in the in-game character creator to get embraced by a random sire
- When achieving Golconda, you now get an alternative option to become mortal. You can either end the game, abdicate and keep playing as your heir, or (if you have Roads to Power) become an Independent Hunter adventurer and keep playing the same character. Turning yourself mortal via the Beatific interaction gives you the same choices
- Parity with the vanilla court positions file. Added the missing court position tasks from vanilla. Added the Court Brewmaster court position for Fianna, Boggans, Satyrs, Independent Hunters, and characters with the Drunkard trait
- Every year AI demons have 15% chance to upgrade their ritual as long they have at least 10 cultists

## Gameplay changes
- Removed the title tier and realm size requirements from the "Become Adventurer" decision
- Wraith binding rework
  - Necromancers now have to weaken the Fetters of a Wraith before they can bind them
  - A necromancer's binding now counts as a Fetter for the Wraith. The amount of these Fetters determines the strength of the hook
  - Overhauled the interaction to command your bound Wraiths with a number of new effects, scaling with the Wraith's stats
- Epidemic tweaks
  - Turned off random non-supernatural epidemics
  - Added a new game rule to adjust the frequency of supernatural epidemics, separate from the vanilla game rule so that it doesn't inherit the setting from other mods. This rule can be changed during an ongoing game
  - Crimson Fever and Chulorviosis no longer reduce development
  - Reverted the anti-epidemic bandaid fix (no more free development gain from cultural innovations)
- Great Persons now receive the "Great Person" trait, making them more easily searchable
- You now need to have at least 25% War contribution to gain Ashen Grandmaster xp when winning a war
- Randomly generated characters can no longer spawn with a tier 5 Prowess education
- The Master Thief camp officer now unlocks the ability to buy artifact claims instead of letting you steal artifacts for free
- When visiting a Grand City holding as an adventurer, you now get all the Castle/City/Church options from vanilla
- You no longer need to travel when hunting a character who's in the same travel entourage as you
- You can now finish certain repeatable Journeys (Hunt in your Capital, Pack Training, Spirit Quest) while leading an army, as a QoL measure since army commanders can teleport anyway
- Tweaked demon objectives
- Umbra duels have been rebalanced, scaling has been lowered
- Umbra duels are no longer always fatal if you lose
- Objectives that require a vampire to be dead or in torpor can now also be completed if the vampire becomes a Wight or is turned into some other splat (e.g. a bound Wraith)
- AI characters progressing in the Golconda Seeker trait track now get some tweaks to their AI values, to make them less likely to commit atrocities the more they leveled up the trait
- Characters that you're currently giving a Golconda mentorship will no longer attempt the Suspire on their own
- Removed the Laham trait from the Ruler Designer since adding it had some unforeseen consequences. If you wanna add it to your custom character, use the debug interaction
- Removed the lifestyle xp bonuses from Clan traits since passive xp gain barely matters for Vampires anyway
- The Ikhwan's starting book is now considered a trinket instead of a royal court book (since they don't start with a royal court)
- Augustus Giovanni will now get the Antediluvian nickname if he achieves the Conspiracy objective 
- Changed the Reconquista struggle hostility reward (which wasn't always a positive) for a force house head one 
- Seal of abamixtra now has a cooldown
- Animal resonance gain from domicile buildings reduced 
- Landless adventurers now start with one more men at arms limit, meaning there should be less potential adventurers combo resulting in starting 0 max MaA limit
- The three convention of thorns interactions now don't require diplomatic range (theme wise, you all are at thorns)
- The 1 stack MaA (like Leviathan, Unnamable etc) now have more stack  #CK3 warfare system isn't kind of 1 entity units. While this is less flavorful, it will make these units pack the punch they should have 
- Werewolf and Bastet buildings now stay enabled (but still can't be built) for kinfolk  #This avoids awkward inheritance, mostly for AI, where buildings are wiped when transferring from a shifter to a kinfolk 
- Opinion bonuses (or penalties, in the case of Giovanni) from drinking blood no longer stack
- Recognize Cultist prestige cost is now dynamic based on arcana perks
- The Chakravarti trait now gives +prestige multiplier instead of bonus to vanilla religions
- The rakish trait now gives -prestige multiplier #Rakish had no drawbacks in PoD otherwise
- Objectives done by the AI are now told to the player in a more limited radius #to avoid, in the future, Japanese rulers being informed of Mithras being deposed 
- House Murnau now has Bavaria color to distinguish it from Eastern Lords 
- The Codex Mortis can no longer be used if you already have necromancy advanced (would do nothing in that case)
- Added a bookmark portrait by Typhon
- An education event assuming you were landed has been disabled for landless rulers 
- Tweaked small snake and giant serpent forms to be less of a clear cut choice 
- The classified information contracts can no longer target unavailable characters 
- Nerfed the veteran adventurer trait
- Disabled two vanilla vassal events needing vanilla contracts to work 
- Commune with the abyss now gives 1 vanilla perk instead of 2. Other rewards not changed 
- Mesmerize cooldown has been reduced 
- Disabled a vanilla event randomly unlocking crusades
- The negative modifiers from the Chancellor route during heists ("Complication: Too Popular") now also decrease courtier opinion, so they aren't free for landless adventurers
- Hunnic culture now once again has access to horse archers
- Buffs to the Gangrel dynasty perks 
- Changed the color of the sept of the night sky to not be the same as its friendly neighbor the voivodate
- Necromancy perks now give some wraiths maa bonus
- You will only usurp the sea of shadows title if it's held by a lasombra now (reward for the reconquista struggle)
- Buffed the Gangrel berserker accolade 
- Vicissitude no longer gives you unboundable (which is a crime to most Tzimisce faiths)
- Reworked the main domicile building and added 2 more ranks to it
- The interaction to give one of your surplus vanilla perk points to another character now gives them the perks directly (because the AI rarely assigns them otherwise)
- Doubled the size but halved the siege value of siege engines (which should result in the same performance but avoid a reinforcement bug)
- Via Venator Umbra (the party animals) now can't raid but are part of the three pillars tolerance
- Removed Ghoul Vassalage doctrines from most non-vampire faiths. Now Ghoul criminality is decided by the Vampirism doctrine when Vampires are not accepted
- Updated the Spanish Galicia cultural setup closer to modern CK3
- Qorjin's Hunters now have the Garou Pacts doctrine instead of Garou Nation
- Added Wyrm Pacts doctrine to Ten Thousand Screams
- True Brujah no longer get credit when the (false) Brujah restore Carthage 
- Buffed the Banu Haqim dynasty perks
- Burmese culture no longer ignore faith opinion modifiers
- Blood Sorcery's Spirit Manipulation tree has been adapted to work with the new spirit rework
- Reduced excessive internal slots in vampire and inquisitor domiciles
- Temple of Osiris in Ancient Cairo has had its max level effect changed to accomodate mummy rework
- Effects that remove clan curses now also work on Gargoyles
- Removed opinion bonuses from vampire faith enlightenment doctrines (Conviction and Self Control/Conscience and Instinct/etc)
- Giving someone a lethal potion now counts as murder
- Refactored code about permanent injuries
- Sneakily renamed the internal IDs for the vanilla Conqueror game rules, to make sure they get set to POD's intended settings even if the player didn't reset game rules to their defaults

