## Translation
- Backported the fix for hiding dynasty names to the Chinese translation (no more Mithras Mithras)
- Added the latest translation upload done by Paratranz users

## Debug
- Added a character interaction in Debug mode to kill a character (allowing for resurrection, unlike the existing debug interaction from vanilla CK3)
- Added a character interaction in Debug mode to give a character various half-splat traits
- The interaction for adding supernatural trait xp now has an option to reduce xp instead

## Bugfixes
- Fixed a long-standing graphical glitch that caused rectangular artifacts in several shaders on Vulkan (e.g. the main menu background)
- Fixed a long-standing graphical glitch that would turn certain types of eyes pixelated with random bright colors
- Objectives that give you a new dynasty legacy no longer deduct its cost from your renown
- Removed some vanilla modifiers that could lead to wars involving conquerors auto ending
- Fixed a number of broken scripts that prevented you from exchanging hostages (both after wars or via character interaction)
- Fae who go to Arcadia during the Shattering now also destroy their titular and Head of Faith titles, to prevent them getting stuck on inaccessible characters
- Fixed the Ashen Grandmaster Holy Order precept not giving any modifiers
- Fixed a bug that would prevent you from executing Wights in your prison
- Giving yourself injury traits in the Ruler Designer now makes them permanent (this is the intended behavior but it seems it got lost during a recent update)
- Fixed KJ characters gaining a few random perks at the start of a game
- Fixed a patron character lacked a splat trait
- Fixed a wrong prerequisite in the Fae Ratkin objective
- Grand Cities no longer will have wrong Special buildings
- Sorcery Heal no longer heals unhealable things
- You no longer can click 'destroy' button on un-destroyable artifacts in GUI
- Non-Shadow Shadow Wraiths no longer count as shadow(for separate kbabit etc.)
- Fixed the weaponized flaying plague staying in your decision tab even after you already done in SH mode 
- Fixed a pilgrimage event that could let you invite hostile splats to your court
- Fixed some gargoyle castes that wouldn't properly get inherited upon embrace
- Revenants now get assigned faiths befitting their bloodline (they always got Via Humanitatis due to an oversight)
- Nirriti Revenants now get Sadhana instead of Thaumaturgy
- Player Demon now correctly gain unkown eminence modifier on startup
- Demon objective 'Demonic Tree of Knowledge' now correctly requires all lore perks, and not arcana.
- Reaper's hunger modifier is now correctly stacks
- Fixed your own capital province switching to tribal when giving a duchy tier or higher title to an unlanded fera
- Heist events will longer select your own Coterie members as adversaries
- AI Beastborn characters can now get heirs
- Fixed some Werewolf special Caerns losing their travel POI after upgrading
- Diablerie will no longer display a random effect that does nothing if your victim has paths from Blood Sorcery or Necromancy that you already know
- Fixed some instances where a character's real age wouldn't be displayed in the UI
- Fixed issues in the KJ unite India objective rewards
- Fixed a vanilla event that could cure Malkavians of depression
- You can no longer launch landless wars on Haven titles
- Great Persons embraced by AI characters now obey all embrace conditions that might apply (e.g. Adisa will only embrace female GPs)
- More safeguards against naked characters breaking the non nudity rule
- Danislav Revenants from the in-game character creator now get the Kinfolk trait
- Fixed a faulty trigger that would let AI Tremere keep accumulating Gargoyles forever and ever
- Added the actual reward thresholds to the description of the landless objective where you visit points of interest
- Postponing the point of interest objective now refunds its cost, like in vanilla
- Fixed various vanilla effects that reward perk points, lifestyle experience, or education upgrades, which didn't do anything for characters who only have a prowess education (they now award martial experience)
- Finally ported scheme agent acceptance to post scheme rework
- Fixed a number of faulty domicile building graphics (e.g. nighttime textures during the day and vice versa)
- Vampires who achieved Golconda can now eat cheese

