- Compatibility with Crusader Kings III 1.16.0.1 "Chamfron" hotfix

## Bugfixes
- Hideout domiciles no longer get cleared by the game periodically (whoops)
- AI Vampires now respect the Ghoul cap instead of gaining more and more of them forever and ever
- Various tributary related fixes
- Fixed Grand City special building not switching
- The "Steal the Power of Vitae" objective now properly gives you a Blood Potency modifier

# Princes of Darkness, "Wind from the East", Version 1.16.0, 4/28/2025

- Compatibility with Crusader Kings III 1.16.0 "Chamfron" update

## Khans of the Steppe 
- Compatibility with the DLC and patch
- The horde DLC system, while possibly worth investigating for PoD hordes, would have taken too much time to integrate with our current schedule (and is completely DLC locked) so is simply disabled
- Raid intents have been adapted for PoD
- Tributaries have been added to PoD with some setup changes to use them
- Our steppe setup has seen some changes to adapt to the new map. It also introduces our PoD lore characters (non canon characters with a lore button to add depth to places with little to no official sources)

## Kuei Jin Rework
- Rework of Dharma mechanic to be more interesting.
- Rework of Kuei Jin lifestyles to be more in-line with modern PoD.
- Rework of Yama Gifts (investiture tree).
- Addition of a new objective to become a Yama King (similar to Decani).
- Removal of Yin/Yang balance trait to reduce complexity.
- Removal of Chi as a resource 
- Tweaking of Hun and P'o in line with new mechanics.
- Adaptation of various miscellaneous mechanics of Kuei Jin, like dhampyr breeding etc to new system.
- Dah modifier now gives +50% Dharma xp gain.
- Umbral modifiers 'Knowledge of Thousand Cranes Mother' and 'Wisdom of Black Pearl Mistress' now instead of lifestyle gain mult gives bi-yearly dharma.
- KJ now have their own domicile buildings
- KJ ducal buildings have been tweaked and no longer require gauntlet manipulation
- Removed the barely used heretical gov form

## Demon Rework
- Removed the Fallen and Earthbound traits and removed the possession mechanic. Demons instead stay on Earth via the Ritual of the Sundered Soul. This modifier is very negative initially but can be improved via decision
- Full rework of the Arcana lifestyle. Most perks cost multiple perk points now
- Full rework of the Lore lifestyle. Its many branches were consolidated into a smaller number of thematically coherent ones
- Resolve now goes from 0-10 (instead of 0-5) and most methods for gaining it were reworked. Revelation is now performed by right-clicking yourself
- Turned the Tempt/Corrupt schemes into a Journey
- Turned the Learn True Name scheme into a Journey (for all splats, not just Demons)
- House Lores are now assigned via dynasty modifier. This means custom characters no longer need to join an existing Demon's dynasty, which fixes some bugs with house head assignment
- Small tweaks to objectives
- Infernalists no longer get a Resolve bar or access to the Arcana lifestyle
- Demons can no longer learn Demonology or gain investments
- Some arcana perks now give access to vanilla schemes
- Tweak to binding/making pact with Demons

## Shih Rework
- Removal of Chi for Shih
- Rework of Qiao
- Rework of Shih Objective(s)
- Added a training journey/mechanic for Shih

## Wheel of Ages Rework
- Change from static dates to dynamic yearly change with thresholds
- Implemented ages 2,3,4,5 and 6 each with corresponding buffs for specific splats/sub-splats.
- Implemented various ways to push Wheel of Ages in both directions.
- Adapted Age objectives for the new system.
- Added game-rule to configure the speed of the Wheel of Ages.

## Grand City of Paris
- Added Paris as a Grand City
  - Chivalric Paris: Available to Ventrue, Toreador, and vampires following Via Equitum. Rebuild Alexander's Grand Court with a slew of unique buildings GC buildings and additional unique buildings available to each of Toreador/Via Equitum, Ventrue, and Alexander himself.
  - Umbral Paris: Available to other vampires and dark supernaturals. Spread your influence over Paris and its people then reap the rewards that follow.
  - Free Paris: Available to everyone else. A Paris freed from the parisitic forces that dwelled in it. The Shadow Inquisition gets unique buildings here.

## Grand City of Cairo
- Added Cairo as a Grand City
  - Ancient Cairo: Available to all members of the Osirian League and Ishmaelite Mummies. Gain unique powers as you gather the Osirians in holy Cairo. You will require all the members as skilled Councillors to unlock the full potential of the city. (This means that both Silent Striders and Bubasti can use this city)
  - Vampiric Cairo: Available to vampires. Build and expand the Khittas to grow Cairo and improve the effectiveness of your councillors and court positions. Faiths with the Ashirra Pillars doctrine gain extra bonuses for building the Ashirra aligned Khittas. Setites can rebuild their founding temples to create their own Road of Set faith.
  - Islamic Cairo: Available to everyone else. But only the Ikhwan al-Safa hunters can unlock the true potential of this city.

## Discipline additions and reworks
- Daimonion rework
  - Includes a new way to unlock the investiture tree in vampire-only bookmarks, and the often requested re embrace ritual
- Flight discipline for Gargoyles

## Gameplay Additions
- Added 6 new Great Persons
- Added an option for Rock Lord to go landless
- Added an experimental game rule that makes AI characters behave more like conquerors
- Added a game rule that lets you hide the likelihood of random outcomes
- For those who missed the April Fools joke from the Patron build, there is now a sneaky game rule to reenable it (only visible if Custom Mode is selected, at the very bottom of the list of game rules)

## Gameplay Changes
- Removed the Gallowsbait trait since it doesn't make sense for this setting. Effects that otherwise would've added Thief or Marauder XP still count as theft for the purposes of Golconda
- Extensive rebalance of shapeshift related modifiers to make them more varied and (hopefully) interesting
- The Animal lifestyle xp from the Stable and Kennels (Vampire domicile building) is now gained passively, regardless of your lifestyle focus. However, this also means it won't benefit from multiplicative xp buffs anymore
- Added a limit to Enhancing based on the artifact's rarity
- You can now become an Ashen Ambassador for unlanded patrons
- Ashen Grandmasters now get 5 trait xp for winning wars (up from 2 xp). This also now applies to contract wars, meaning you can double-dip them for 10 xp
- Tripled the xp rewards and prestige cost of the Ambassadorial Visit interaction
- Giving land to your Ambassadorial Patron via the landless CB now gives trait xp, based on the title tier
- Removed the Hive Mind, Renegades, and Celestial Army government types
- Infernalists now keep a splat-appropriate government type if possible, instead of switching to the Infernal Court government every time. This also fixes a bug where Vampire infernalists would lose their domicile
- Diablerie via draining a herd member or using the cannibalism execution option now fires the same suspicion event as the diablerie execution option
- Adventurers (like Dracula) or the Grandmasters from the Age of the Inquisition now get all the necessary scripts for Conqueror behavior, not just the trait. This means they're somewhat more difficult, but also that they can lose the trait (e.g. if they repeatedly lose wars or go into big debt)
- Reactivated the adventurer interaction from vanilla that lets you switch sides during a war. Backstab away (within reason, you can't circumvent splat hostility this way)
- Genetic intellect traits now count as Fame traits for the purposes of trait-editing abilities, meaning that abilities that only change physical traits (e.g. Will over Form) can no longer turn anyone into a genius
- Removed a number of nonsensical fame traits from Reweaving (e.g. Sayyid or Saoshyant Descendant)
- Increased the prestige cost of Prison of Water. Also, Conquerors are now immune
- If you were to defeat a certain [FLUFFY ANIMAL] at the end of the [PETTING ZOO] and it were, for some reason, able to resurrect, it would now do so. It won't, of course, because it can't. That would be silly. Wouldn't it
- The healing sorcery tree now gives some epidemic resistance
- Strengthen bloodline vanilla decision no longer gives a nickname 
- Some Kuei Jin objectives no longer check for barons while looking for validity
- Shih can't convert faith via the usual panel anymore (doing so break their stuff)
- Chimerstry battle modifiers have been replaced by a new, more war focused, effect  #To avoid your economy crashing each time Chandraputra looks funny at you
- Effigy battle modifiers have been replaced by buffs for your constructs #The battle modifiers debuffing enemy constructs were basically useless. Now instead you can buff your Ushabti to even more greater heights 
- Added some provisions mult to ashen caravan domicile building
- The indep hunter objective option that focuses on sorcery now makes magick accepted by the indep hunter faith as a whole
- Absorb/devour the mind has been reworked to actually work properly. And also nerfed to remove a base stat when used
- You can now become a Cardinal for the Sabbat as a vassal, as long as your liege is the Regent
- You now lose the Psychic trait and lifestyle perks if you switch to a splat that doesn't have access to psychic powers
- Buffed the Scheme speed buff from Flow with the Mountain (Visceratika perk)
- Removed the opinion penalty from Create Name (Obfuscate elder perk)
- Enabled the Knight-Errant landless objective for Via Equitum
- The end of ages objective now also works if you took the required titles instead of destroying them
- Many minor and major tweaks to Enchanting(sorcery)
- Added the Laham trait to the Ruler Designer (at an exorbitant cost, like other traits that otherwise take some effort to achieve)
- Added mythical animal shapeshifts to Archmaster Shapeshifting (Sorcery perk)
- Ashirra court positions completely reworked and now have court position tasks
- Characters with Osirian League faiths can now always interact with each other, bypassing other splat hostility checks
- Sorcery, Blood Magic and Necromancy success chance is no longer depended on distance between caster and target
- Added tooltip to Decani Objective, warning players about challange they will face
- Tweaked a death by thirst travel event to not kill immortals anymore
- Tweaked the Bubasti objective to target another county (Qus already has a wonder so couldn't get the reward)
- Bastet court positions aptitude prerequisites lowered to make it easier to unlock their buildings
- Shapeshifters as a whole can now build the unique caerns and not just werewolves
- Spirit companions now gives charm lifestyle xp mult passively. Removed the interaction to send spirits to randomly fetch charms perk for you
- Gargoyles created via the Gargoyle dynasty tree perk will now be the faith of their creator and not via servilis
- You now gain fewer "free buildings" when conquering another splat's county 
- Dynasty/house head call to arms has been disabled #Neither made much sense in PoD where our dynasties are massive and worldwide
- Golconda Seekers/Achievers can no longer recruit Szlachta or Vozhd

## History
- Added Bezariel's conspiracy 
- Added 3 portraits
- CN DA Tremere full read (new characters, coterie, lore button etc)
- Gave Cappadocian Necromancy to a few Patron characters who were missing a tradition (contact us if you want a different one for your character)
- Shaved Yuri's beard
- Antonius of Cairo now starts with the Tariq el-Harb faith and the cynical trait
- Cairo starts with the Tariq el-Sama faith

## Interface
- The Hideout's main building now uses estate graphics for landed characters. Also, the description was changed to clarify that this is a collection of moveable assets and not a literal building
- When you install a new ruler via the landless CB, there's now a checkbox to show only pinned characters (from the Outliner) in the list
- Characters with interaction blockers (e.g. hostile splats) now show you that blocker in the interaction menu, with an explanation in the tooltip
- Added a mod compatibility warning if window_domicile.gui is overwritten
- Added a warning at the start of the game if one of your mods overwrites vanilla traits
- POD Lore button: These characters were created by PoD Developers to add greater depth to the setting and are not an official part of the World of Darkness.

## Graphics
- Landed owners hideout estate domiciles have building not tent graphics.
- The camps and hideout estate domiciles of undead characters have night time graphics.
- Added 50 nighttime versions of vanilla event backgrounds to events and the Barbershop
- Edited 4 existing nighttime event backgrounds to have more cinematic lighting instead of literal pitch blackness
- Regenerated the bookmark portraits since Paradox fixed beauty gene constraints in the DLC. Characters who got a distorted face after Roads to Power got their old faces back (Helena enjoyers rejoice)
- Nosferatu from the Ruler Designer no longer get Nosferatu looks forced upon them. Instead, you get an event 1 day after game start where you can choose to keep their appearance, or get random deformations as normal

## Optimization
- Removed regent succession to make the game run faster (it was the most performance-intensive script in the game even though we don't need it)

## Translation
- Chinese localization updated

## Debug
- Added a character interaction in Debug Mode to add trait xp for supernatural traits
- Added a character interaction in Debug Mode to change the clothing colors of other characters
- Added a character interaction in Debug Mode to learn the Spell of Life

## Bugfixes
- Fixed a bug that could cause abilities that read your base stats (e.g. Shadow Twin) to raise your base stats permanently
- Big cleanup of interaction triggers. This fixes a lot of cases of nonsensical characters (e.g. Wights or Zombu) showing up in events, being hireable in court positions, and the like
- Claimant factions now work again
- Changed the income modifiers from your hideout to domicile income modifiers, so that they properly work with domicile income multipliers
- Fixed a bug that would cause domicile buildings to get lost on succession under certain circumstances
- Barons no longer marry. They got up to too many shenanigans
- If you become immortal after the Know Thyself perk warned you of your impending natural death, you will no longer die anyway
- Executions via exsanguination or cannibalism no longer kill their victims twice, so they won't mess with resurrection abilities
- Fix for characters dying permanently in Tournaments despite having resurrection abilities
- AI vampires will no longer build generic camp buildings in their domiciles
- Kinfolk and Kinain potions now warn about their lethality
- Kinfolk and Kinain sacrifice methods no longer give modifiers
- Fixed a bug where you could select the wrong type of sacrifice when crafting
- Becoming a vampire now clears existing blood potency modifiers, so that certain edge cases (e.g. ghouls drinking a vampire potion) don't result in characters with multiple blood potency modifiers
- Fixed an event that would build a vanilla domicile building, even if your splat shouldn't have access to those
- You can no longer use Lay on Hands without selecting an option
- AI characters can now offer you concubines (they couldn't because of a malformed trigger, whoops)
- Natural-born characters now get a resonance assigned on their 16th birthday (when their personality is in place)
- Changed a couple of events that could give Sorcery to ineligible splats
- Some additional safeguards so that adventurers can't donate titles to characters that shouldn't receive them (e.g. mercenary captains or spiritual heads of faith)
- Master Assassins now speed up your schemes instead of slowing them down
- Turning a vampire into a mortal via max-rank Beatific now gets rid of their old family relations. In case you want to embrace your sire or something
- Yearly heal for any health issues, is now correctly limited to shih with perk.
- Fix for random Vampires on Roguelike Mode not getting any disciplines
- Fixed a bunch of splat-switching events that would lead to a game over for landless adventurers because they forced a landed government type on you
